# Copy to `.env` and edit. Every value is OPTIONAL — the server boots without it.
# Authoring a module needs NO configuration at all; only publishing needs a token.

# --- This server (JMC_ prefix, see src/just_module_creator/settings.py) -------

# Registry tokens — ONE PER INSTANCE. Production and the polygon keep separate
# databases, so an account on one does not exist on the other and neither token
# is a fallback for the other. For multi-user HTTP prefer the per-request
# `X-Registry-Token` / `X-Registry-Test-Token` headers or the `authenticate`
# tool. These fall back to REGISTRY_TOKEN / REGISTRY_TEST_TOKEN (below).
# No account yet? `registry_register` mints one per instance and hands you both
# secrets — register on each with the SAME install-id.
# JMC_API_KEY=            # production
# JMC_TEST_API_KEY=       # the polygon (target="test")

# The proof-of-work install-id your account was registered with.
#
# SAVE IT HERE. It is the account's ONLY recovery path: the registry has no email
# and no admin, so re-registering this exact id is the one way to get a fresh key
# for the same account. Register again without it and you create a DIFFERENT
# account, leaving the first one unreachable forever.
#
# `registry_register` reads this when you pass no install_id, so a later session
# reissues a key instead of stranding the account.
# JMC_INSTALL_ID=

# There is no tool surface setting. JMC_MODE and the `extended` tier were removed
# in 0.21.0: every tool is registered on every start. The expensive ones — the
# citation graph, the PGx drafters, the bulk fact passes — say what they cost in
# their own descriptions instead of being hidden from the sessions that need them.

# Hide the token-gated registry tools from a session until it calls `authenticate`.
# Default false: listed-but-refusing keeps them discoverable by an agent that has
# no token, and the refusal says how to get one. Hidden, a call by name gets
# "Unknown tool" instead. Worth turning on for a shared HTTP deployment; leave it
# off for authoring.
# JMC_HIDE_GATED_UNTIL_AUTH=false

# Two-layer tool surface. flat (default) lists all 57 tools — measured at 61,458
# tokens, 31% of a 200k context window. layered lists the core authoring loop and
# holds nine named groups behind the `toolbox` tool, which rosters them and reveals
# one to the asking session: 20,103 tokens, a 67% saving. Nothing is unreachable
# and the roster is always readable, which is the difference from the tier that was
# removed. It defaults OFF because a mid-session reveal needs a client that honours
# notifications/tools/list_changed; without one, a revealed group appears after a
# reconnect.
# JMC_TOOLBOX=flat

# Tool discovery. off (default) lists every tool; regex|bm25 replace the listing
# with search_tools + call_tool so a client finds tools by querying. It narrows
# what is LISTED, never what is callable — an unlisted tool is still callable by
# name, which is what makes this different from the tier that was removed.
# `registry_register` and `authenticate` stay listed either way.
# JMC_TOOL_SEARCH=off
# JMC_TOOL_SEARCH_MAX_RESULTS=5

# Hard network ceiling. When true, every tool that could fetch runs cache-only
# and a per-call `offline=false` cannot override it.
# JMC_OFFLINE=false

# Refuse to read or write outside this directory. Unset = no restriction.
# JMC_WORKSPACE=

# The two registry endpoints. `target="prod"` uses the first, `target="test"`
# the second. The write tools default to the polygon, where a publish is a
# rehearsal that `registry_delete_version` can undo; production is immutable and
# its content claim is never released.
# JMC_REGISTRY_URL=https://module-registry.just-dna.life
# JMC_REGISTRY_TEST_URL=https://module-polygon.just-dna.life
# JMC_REGISTRY_TIMEOUT=600

# Transport + bind address for network transports.
# JMC_TRANSPORT=stdio        # stdio | http | sse
# JMC_HOST=127.0.0.1
# JMC_PORT=3011

# Logging level for server-side logs (written to stderr).
# JMC_LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# Header names used to read a per-request registry token over HTTP. Two, so one
# client can drive both instances without the second call reusing the first
# instance's credential.
# JMC_API_KEY_HEADER=X-Registry-Token
# JMC_TEST_API_KEY_HEADER=X-Registry-Test-Token

# --- The just-dna toolchain's own environment --------------------------------
# Read by the enricher itself, straight from the process environment. This
# server neither reads nor forwards them; set them here so an author configures
# everything in one place.

# REGISTRY_TOKEN=                          # what registry-client already uses
# REGISTRY_TEST_TOKEN=                     # the same, for the polygon
# JUST_DNA_PIPELINES_CACHE_DIR=            # base for all snapshot caches
#   SET THIS. Unset is not "no cache" — it silently falls back to platformdirs
#   (~/.cache/just-dna-pipelines), and the Ensembl snapshot alone is ~14 GB. On
#   2026-08-31 that filled a root filesystem to 91% mid-benchmark. Point it at a
#   volume with room: JUST_DNA_PIPELINES_CACHE_DIR=/data/just-dna-cache
# JUST_DNA_ENSEMBL_CACHE=
# JUST_DNA_CLINVAR_CACHE=
# JUST_DNA_GNOMAD_CONSTRAINT_CACHE=
# NCBI_API_KEY=                            # tightens PubMed/dbSNP pacing to 1/10s
# JUST_DNA_CONTACT_EMAIL=                  # polite-pool contact for NCBI/EuropePMC
#                                          # (read second — see JMC_USER_EMAIL below)
# PHARMVAR_API_KEY=                        # PERSONAL under PharmVar ToS §2 —
#                                          # never bake it into a module or snapshot

# --- Literature discovery -----------------------------------------------------
# Which third-party literature services this deployment may talk to. A policy
# ceiling shaped like JMC_OFFLINE: a per-call `sources` argument narrows it and
# can never widen it. Unset means every source; an empty value means none, and
# the two are deliberately different answers.
#   JMC_LITERATURE_SOURCES=pubmed,europepmc,semanticscholar,preprints
# JMC_LITERATURE_SOURCES=

# Semantic Scholar raises the rate limit for a keyed caller. Absent means
# unauthenticated and slower, never unavailable. Read from JMC_S2_API_KEY, else
# S2_API_KEY (the name S2's own docs use).
# JMC_S2_API_KEY=

# --- Who is calling: PLEASE SET THIS -----------------------------------------
# NCBI's polite pool and Unpaywall both meter *and* contact per address, so this
# is not decoration — it says whose rate-limit budget is being spent and who gets
# emailed if something goes wrong.
#
# Resolved in three steps, first hit wins:
#   1. JMC_USER_EMAIL            yours
#   2. JUST_DNA_CONTACT_EMAIL    the enricher's own variable (above), so one
#                                .env still configures both surfaces
#   3. just.dna.seq@gmail.com    the project's address, as a last resort
#
# Step 3 is why nothing here ever reports "no contact configured" any more, and
# it is also the reason to set step 1. Leaving it unset pools your traffic with
# every other unconfigured install under one identity — you share that rate
# limit, and an abuse report caused by your usage lands in the project's inbox
# rather than yours. One line fixes it.
#
# What has NOT changed: an address is never *invented*. The default is the
# project's own, given by its owner; a made-up one would misattribute traffic to
# a stranger, and that stays forbidden.
# JMC_USER_EMAIL=
